  body: "# Benefit payment arrangements in the DMG\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe captured chapter describes
    arrangements for paying benefit, including nominated accounts, appointees and benefit-specific guidance routes.\n\
    \n## Scope and exceptions\n\nAn award, the amount payable and the payment arrangement are distinct. DMG 08002
    routes UC, PIP and new-style ESA/JSA payment to ADM B1; this batch does not apply the DMG procedure to those
    benefits.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 08002, PDF page 3](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/66fd5bbbe84ae1fd8592ecf1/dmg-chapter-8-payment-of-benefit-and-deductions-from-benefit.pdf#page=3)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 8: Payment of benefit and deductions from benefit .\n- [DMG 08007, PDF page 4](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/66fd5bbbe84ae1fd8592ecf1/dmg-chapter-8-payment-of-benefit-and-deductions-from-benefit.pdf#page=4)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 8: Payment of benefit and deductions from benefit .\n- [DMG 08010, PDF page 4](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/66fd5bbbe84ae1fd8592ecf1/dmg-chapter-8-payment-of-benefit-and-deductions-from-benefit.pdf#page=4)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 8: Payment of benefit and deductions from benefit .\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted
    interpretation of the 15 September 2026 source snapshot; unreviewed and requiring specialist review. The source
    is DWP guidance, not a consolidated statement of legislation. This is an independent experimental publication,
    not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule.\n\nPDF page numbers are
    one-based file positions. Machine extraction can alter reading order, footnotes and characters. Quoted relationships
    preserve extracted text; no visual or specialist acceptance is claimed. Source dates, legal effects and current
    applicability remain separate review tasks.\n\n- `dmg-vol3-ch8` PDF SHA-256: `8bf08435715020c8cc57be24e06e6fd8c90d99232254004ba67d1c5dfc3dd864`;
    extracted pages SHA-256: `e6c5a71afbf2536bc63a91a4389284b2b6b8aaaa8bff015d4f34b478f77b28cc`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/pension-credit
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source explicitly points payment research for SPC to chapter 79; this does not equate all
      benefits’ payment rules.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol3-ch8/0003
      quote: "08002 Guidance on payment of benefit follows but other guidance on this subject may be found in\n\
        benefit specific DMG Chapters:-\n\n\n1. IS/JSA Chapter 33\n\n\n2. ESA Chapter 46\n\n\n3. AA/DLA Chapter
        61\n\n\n4. SPC Chapter 79.\n\n\nNote 1: ADM Chapter B1 contains guidance on the payment of UC, PIP, new
        style ESA and new style JSA.\n\n\nNote 2: ADM Chapter M1 contains guidance on the meaning of new style ESA
        and new style JSA."
      locator: DMG 08002
